{
  "_note": "Single source of truth for llm-opd-token-signal's ONE training run and its three scored evaluations (2026-09-30 redesign: train one model and evaluate it on several datasets). The task is Delta OPD regime 2: the student learns the teacher's post-training delta T - R, where R is the teacher's own base, and the point is that this delta transfers even when the teacher is NOT stronger than the student. So the teacher is WEAKER than the student: a small post-trained model (Qwen3-0.6B) teaching a larger student (Qwen3-1.7B), with the reference being that teacher's OWN base (Qwen3-0.6B-Base), so T - R is exactly its post-training delta while T - S points at a weaker model. Measured precondition: teacher 0.3197 vs untouched student 0.5158 on the identical eval path, 19.6 points weaker. The strong-teacher settings (math / code / mathgap, teacher Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507) and samesize were REMOVED because they reward following a stronger teacher, the opposite of the question. The completion cap is 4096 for training AND eval (a 1024 cap truncated 90-96% of teacher-informed math rollouts, measured). `trainings` maps a training label stem to its run; `evals` maps each *_eval label stem to the training run whose checkpoint it scores and the held-out benchmark(s) it scores it on. Every eval of one training run loads the SAME checkpoint ($OUTPUT_DIR/<training>).",
  "trainings": {
    "weakteacher": {
      "domain": "math",
      "student": "Qwen3-1.7B",
      "teacher": "Qwen3-0.6B",
      "reference": "Qwen3-0.6B-Base",
      "completion": 4096
    }
  },
  "evals": {
    "weakteacher_math500": {"training": "weakteacher", "benches": ["math500"]},
    "weakteacher_olympiadbench": {"training": "weakteacher", "benches": ["olympiadbench"]},
    "weakteacher_amc23": {"training": "weakteacher", "benches": ["amc23"]}
  }
}

